body:
Sorry to reopen this, but I have similar problem for varchar and text, probably more types. Don't really know whats causing this.

During restart I got this
```
query: ALTER TABLE `user` DROP COLUMN `token`
query: ALTER TABLE `user` ADD `token` text NOT NULL
```

And boom, all tokens gone. I tried different lengths but I'm lost, don't know what to try next.
Im using nest.js and my Entity is as follows:
```
@Entity()
export class User {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn({ type: 'int' })
  userId: number;
  @Column({ nullable: false, length: 255, type: 'varchar' })
  password: string;
  @Column({ type: 'text' })
  token: string;
  @Column({ unique: true, nullable: false, length: 255, type: 'varchar' })
  login: string;
}
```
typeorm version ^0.2.16

This is happening for me as well, 0.2.18.

```
@Entity()
export class Prototype {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
  id: number;

  @Column({
    // unique: false,
    nullable: true,
  })
  description: string;

}
```
